  "asr_text": "At the breakfast table, beside the pillow in the nurse's office, and when work messages come, people want to stay able to talk to the other person. The school's phone collection might reduce arguments over the basket at night, but it could cut off a conversation by the pillow. It might protect learning in class, but if it also stops messages about shifts during breaks, trust at work could be shaken. The father asking the school for help also doesn't want to go through the silence after taking the phone away again. They may disagree about how long phones should be handed in, but they share a wish to still have someone they can talk to. What message do you want to answer right away? When does it come, and who sends it?",
